{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/y90nupkv","slide":1,"text":"Expanded candidate model based on the user-provided BRIGHT_model_MoAT_palette_v4.pptx. Source images retained. BRIGHT inputs: Chen et al., ESSD 2025, doi:10.5194/essd-17-6217-2025, Fig. 6 Turkey event, imagery credits Table 2. Output image provenance as a model prediction is not established, so it remains Example map. Q is pixel-to-region soft assignment; T=Pool(F,Q); local interaction produces deltaT_local and T_A=T+deltaT_local. Projection and Q-unpool produce pixel-space deltaF_local, then F_A=F+deltaF_local. Building pool and projection produce key k_b. Top-K searches only eligible training supports, enforcing source restrictions and deduplication. During inference the train-only memory remains active. V_j is the support-local token set (attention keys and values); T_A is the query. Attention weights are shared over j. U_j is query-aligned local evidence. Support label embedding e(y_j) and mask m_j enter support aggregation, not local ground truth. Source IDs are used for eligibility filtering. Projection and Q-unpool produce deltaF_mem. Zero legal support produces zero increment. Memory refresh, differentiability of retrieval, training exclusion, and choice of event restrictions must be defined in the implementation. No new performance or novelty claim is made."}